    "alert_id": "METABOLIC_SYNDROME_002",
    "title": "New Metabolic Syndrome",
    "message": "Patient has developed multiple components of metabolic syndrome since ART switch: impaired fasting glucose (118 mg/dL), pre-diabetic HbA1c (6.1%), dyslipidemia (LDL 148 mg/dL, TG 212 mg/dL), elevated BP (138/88 mmHg), and central obesity (waist 96 cm). Acanthosis nigricans is a cutaneous marker of insulin resistance. This cluster increases cardiovascular risk. Weight gain on DTG may be a contributing factor, but family history of type 2 diabetes is also relevant.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
