    "title": "Missing Glucose Monitoring Plan",
    "message": "Guidelines recommend glucose monitoring every 3 months for the first year for people living with HIV transitioned to DTG. The patient switched to TLD (DTG-based) 18 months ago. While she now has impaired fasting glucose and pre-diabetes, there is no documented plan for ongoing glycemic monitoring or management in the clinician's assessment.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Implement guideline-recommended glucose monitoring every 3 months and document a management plan for pre-diabetes.",
